            <div xml:id="d765">

                <pb facs="0969" n="959" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg959"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4–1647</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the Navy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Forrestal</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-04-16">April 16, 1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Referring to your letter
                    of April 9, I have been informed by Commander Naval Forces, Western Pacific,
                    that Nationalist authorities were to be notified on April 14 of our intentions
                    to abandon the ammunition dumps at HsinHo and at airfield Peiping. He estimated
                    that the Nationalist troops could assume responsibilities for guarding this
                    ammunition by April 21.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Forrestal</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
